{"kind":"artifact","text":"End-to-end walkthrough: the merge step now keeps the successor's identity.\n\nSuccessor at this path for head 66bf2404, answering review's finding 1. The walkthrough created the merged artifact, threw away its EventID, and retired the branch artifact with nothing naming what replaced it — then asked the retired artifact for its provenance in the audit step. A reader following that chain arrives at a dead end holding prose about a successor they cannot resolve, which is precisely the failure the page exists to teach against.\n\nIt now captures MERGED_ARTIFACT, passes it as --rests-on before the positional target, and audits the live artifact. The flag order is load-bearing twice: gs supersede puts the target first in the basis itself so the flag carries only the successor, and flag parsing stops at the first positional.\n\nThe frontmatter is repaired as well. It rested on three comma-joined pseudo-paths — the exact shape this page's own text says cannot participate in succession. It now rests on the live cmd/gs artifact, the CLI it walks through.\n\nNothing at this path was retired when a4f4a57a's artifact was published against it, so that predecessor is retired here.\n\n`go test ./internal/docset -count=1` passes at this head, and the gate runs these commands rather than reading them — it is what caught the flag-order defect in the first place.","body":{"commit":"66bf24046b4f4a466dedaabdf06896497f708375","path":"docs/how-to/end-to-end.md"}}